          <p>
            These are rough estimates, and body proportions vary by several inches either way:
            measure your own elbow height in shoes before you buy. Two points stand out. First, even
            the tallest desk here leaves walkers over about six feet short on most pads, which is a
            limitation of the standing desk market rather than these models; taller users should
            pair a desk like the E6 MAX with the slimmest pad they can find, or look for a frame that
            lists a maximum above 50 inches. Second, the budget desks suit shorter walkers well, and
            there is no reason for a 5 ft 2 in. walker on a slim pad to pay for three-stage legs.
          </p>
